# Desktop routing — SELKIES stack. Provisioned at build time into
# /etc/caddy/desktop.d/ and glob-imported by the main Caddyfile when
# DESKTOP_STACK includes selkies. Owns /desktop/ (runs parallel to /vnc/).
#
# Selkies is WS-ONLY on :6080 (does NOT serve the web client). Caddy serves the
# static client from /usr/share/selkies/web and reverse-proxies only the WebSocket.
# The client opens <path>/websockets (plural).
#
# AUTH: both the static client AND the WebSocket are now behind the UNIFIED AUTH GATEWAY
# (the forward_auth session gate in the main Caddyfile runs before this snippet). Selkies itself
# has no auth of its own and none is needed here: the session cookie is required to reach either
# /desktop/ or /desktop/websockets, and the cookie rides the WS upgrade. This closes the former
# hole (unauthenticated WS = free desktop stream + input) as a property of the perimeter rather
# than a per-snippet patch. Do NOT re-add a basic_auth here — it cannot gate the JS WebSocket and
# would only add a redundant prompt on the static page.

# (1) WebSocket — must come BEFORE the static handler (longer path = higher priority).
@desktop_ws path /desktop/websockets
handle @desktop_ws {
	uri strip_prefix /desktop
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:6080
}

# (2) Static client — Caddy file_server serves the dashboard (gated upstream by the session gate).
handle_path /desktop/* {
	root * /usr/share/selkies/web
	file_server
}
handle /desktop {
	redir /desktop/ permanent
}
